---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import Panel from "~/components/illustration-kit/Panel.astro"
import SvgFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/SvgFigure.astro"
import { series, stroke } from "~/data/palette"
---

<IllustrationFigure
  name="prosecutors-fallacy"
  lead="A rare match does not mean guilt is nearly certain."
>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <Panel class="text-center">
      <p class="text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums">100,000</p>
      <p class="text-base">Possible suspects</p>
    </Panel>
    <Panel class="text-center">
      <p class="text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums">About 100</p>
      <p class="text-base">People who match</p>
    </Panel>
    <Panel class="text-center">
      <p class="text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums">1</p>
      <p class="text-base">Actual culprit</p>
    </Panel>
  </div>

  <p class="text-base font-bold">Here are the roughly 100 people who match the evidence:</p>
  <SvgFigure
    name="prosecutors-fallacy-matches"
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-xs"
    viewBox="0 0 220 220"
    title="One culprit among about a hundred matching people"
    desc="A grid of one hundred squares represents roughly one hundred people who match the trace. One outlined blue square marks the culprit. The other ninety-nine gold squares represent innocent people who also match."
  >
    {Array.from({ length: 100 }, (_, i) => (
      <rect
        x={6 + (i % 10) * 21}
        y={6 + Math.floor(i / 10) * 21}
        width="16"
        height="16"
        fill={i === 0 ? series.blue : series.gold}
        stroke={i === 0 ? stroke : "none"}
        stroke-width={i === 0 ? 2 : 0}
      />
    ))}
  </SvgFigure>

  <ul class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-base">
    <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 border-2 border-ink bg-series-blue" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      1 culprit
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 bg-series-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      About 99 innocent matches
    </li>
  </ul>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    Suppose the trace matches 1 in 1,000 innocent people. If 100,000 people are equally likely
    suspects and there are no other clues, about 100 would match, including the culprit. If a
    person is chosen from those matches, the chance that person is guilty is roughly 1%, not
    99.9%. The match is useful evidence, but it does not settle guilt on its own.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
